{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-05T04:32:30.577Z","author":"pi-glm","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.3:cloud","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"689bbe7fc95ee538aa40a16a","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.3:cloud","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-rl-od32"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"Durable loop continuation: idempotent resume, controller lease, cancellation drills"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Make the persisted recursive loop durable and crash-safe. pm rl loop run becomes idempotent: re-running after a crash at ANY phase (collect, train, evaluate, promote) never double-counts the sample budget, never re-promotes, and never loses an artifact; every partially persisted generation is completed from its persisted evidence. Add pm rl loop status <id> (read-only reconstruction) and pm rl loop resume <id> (resume from the persisted programme). Two controllers racing to launch the same loop produce exactly one job: the launch is guarded by the pm SDK's own primitives — an owner-bound claim on the loop seed plus the SDK workspace lock (acquireLock), with dead-holder takeover — never an invented lock file; proven by a real two-process test. SIGINT/SIGTERM/AbortSignal mid-phase leave consistent state that a resume completes to the identical uninterrupted result."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Feature"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":1},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["durability","execution","recursive-training"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-10-05T04:32:30.577Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-05T04:32:30.577Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"pi-glm"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":960},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"pm rl loop run re-run after an injected failure at each phase boundary completes to the exact uninterrupted report, with one create per item in history and no duplicated metric events; pm rl loop status reports per-generation phase, consumed budget and terminal reason without mutating anything; pm rl loop resume completes an interrupted loop from the persisted seed configuration; two concurrent controller processes produce exactly one seed, one run per generation and one promotion, the loser failing with a stable contention error; a killed controller's lease is taken over promptly via dead-pid detection; AbortSignal/SIGTERM cancellation mid-phase stops at a phase boundary, leaves consistent state, and a subsequent resume completes the loop"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-rl-apvf"}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"32bb1bd4b4b029f0d504e09056cee9cfcc7089f7de77d5a85080a00df671f456","item_hash_version":3,"message":"","event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"7b8a11c1ff7c78c7c268d537a0b6e8f5dfea18ad158703eb6c47817eb9a44ae2"}
