{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-05T04:32:45.155Z","author":"pi-glm","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.3:cloud","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"689bbe7fc95ee538aa40a16a","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.3:cloud","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-05T04:32:45.155Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-10-05T04:32:45.155Z","author":"pi-glm","text":"Starting the durable-continuation slice on branch feat/durable-rsi-continuation. Design decisions recorded as I go: (1) launch mutual exclusion uses the pm SDK's own primitives — an owner-bound claim on the loop seed item plus the SDK workspace lock acquireLock per generation, with dead-pid takeover of an abandoned SDK lock record; no invented lock file. (2) resume reconstructs state from persisted items only: the deterministic bandit receipt is recomputed and verified against the stored training configuration, and missing metric-event suffixes are appended rather than re-collected. (3) pm rl loop run becomes idempotent end to end; the previous loop_already_started refusal is replaced by resume semantics, while a different configuration under the same loop id still conflicts through the content-addressed registration identity."}]}],"before_hash":"0eeb0ab293596c12cc8a79f47de2cbaeb29de8ba717886ef77d5c18793522558","after_hash":"53e768e89f7f92497146eac35d2b68213d140d35762313cc796985b24e7e776f","item_hash_version":3,"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"0897a493d80f9c5eb85ae2ded4db6f16b178deae1d9d485975e8d6049da05fe7"}
